{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/92387-ways-hunters-hear-about-targets","id":92387,"title":"Ways Hunters Hear About Targets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-16T12:12:10-07:00","id":92387,"title":"Ways Hunters Hear About Targets","content":"I've been kinda struggling, here: How do Hunters find out about targets they need to take out without that information being super public? For Conspiracies, it's a little more straight forward, since they can simply receive orders or have relatively vast networks of information gathering. But for Compacts, it seems a little more rough -- do they just have their ear pressed firmly to the ground, with a multitude of local contacts, or do they rely on &quot;suspicious&quot; news reports and so forth? If the latter, how is it they can tell something's amiss without it basically being public knowledge that something odd is happening? Or is that just the basic reality of the World of Darkness: people don't want to know that something is wrong, so they ignore it?<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose the core of my struggle comes from either how CWoD did things, or how the group that introduced me to CWoD did things: that everything is hush-hush, everything is covered up. But I kind of get the impression that this isn't the case in nWoD (or never was in CWoD). The story of how Night Watch started up, for instance, has a few people set fire to a Vampire Haven as basically the entire neighborhood looks on and cheers, which either means that this was a special fringe case that pops up occasionally or that even non-Hunter mortals understand that there's just a constant barrage of weird shit happening around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:31:33-07:00","id":92397,"title":"","content":"You've got it right, really - hunters who don't receive orders or information from somewhere else need to simply pay attention to things that happen in their area that might be caused by monsters, and then investigate to find out if that's really the case. Which means that yes, lack of proper intelligence and acting blind are both big problems for many hunter cells. Likewise, hunters being ignorant of monsters right under their noses or going off on a wild goose chase where no supernaturals are involved are both situations that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T16:17:29-07:00","id":92524,"title":"","content":"When I ran Hunter, the PCs belonged to a private detective firm that was investigating what happened to their founder. Unraveling this mystery formed the basis of the Chronicle along with some PC specific subplots. <br /> <br /> The supernatural is secretive but PCs by their nature are the sort to stumble across the interesting stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/463-derendel","name":"Derendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T08:14:04-07:00","id":92792,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T02:04:18-07:00","id":94176,"title":"","content":"I think my best example, is the first Hunter quest i was a part of. In that one, each of us had alot of different contacts and connections in places, particularily my character who was the knowledge/contact guy. My character worked at as a professor of languages and history at a university, and had been an arkeologist when he was younger, so he knew a shit loud of people. Whenever they told him anything wierd, in passing, he'de pass it on to the Cell and they would go to investigate.<br /> <br /> Another character had a criminal history, and whenever one of the other thugs he knew told him about some guy having lived through a vigorous beating or several gun shots, that was course for concern.<br /> <br /> A third character was part of the church, though not a fanatic. Whenever he heard any of his more fanatical co-members talk of a posession or generally someone who was &quot;corrupting the youth&quot;, we'de poke our attention at it. This lead to the Cell attending a drug fueled Rave once, because a church member had been convinced the DJ was a demonic Succubus sent to corrupt the next generation...<br /> <br /> And lastly, we just generally kept our eyes and ears open to the pieces of media, that might otherwise go relatively unnoticed. A disappearance, strange phenoma, people claiming that they've heard strange noises from the march at night. We did turn up empty handed a few times, one especially funny case in which we investigated a suposed &quot;haunted house&quot; (which was a turist attraction), and ended up getting ourselves lost when we left the group to scout for &quot;demons&quot; or whatever.<br /> But to me, thats some of the fun. Even in the World of Darkness, not everything is of the supernal. And as a hunter, no matter how balanced and calm you might appear, you are, at your core, a paranoid fuckwit, on a binge crusade to rid the world of nasties, the precise definition of which vary greatly from hunter to hunter. So you do end up making alot of assumptions and guesses, which hardly always turns out to be right.<br /> Our cell never ended up killing a civillian by mistake, but if i ran a Hunter quest myself, that would certainly be something i would bring up, if my group behaved like we did.<br /> <br /> This has been a long smear that basically amounts to &quot;It varies&quot;, but i hope it helped, however minuscule it might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T12:00:44-07:00","id":94368,"title":"","content":"That certainly helped! Really, anything like that is good. That all certainly sounds like fun and I might be stealing a little bit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:43:14-07:00","id":94510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/92387-ways-hunters-hear-about-targets?p=94176#post94176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And as a hunter, no matter how balanced and calm you might appear, you are, at your core, a paranoid fuckwit, on a binge crusade to rid the world of nasties, the precise definition of which vary greatly from hunter to hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a highly accurate statement which needs to be kept firmly in mind when playing and running Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T16:19:31-07:00","id":94531,"title":"","content":"It's really not. Hunter is one of the most diverse games at all the nWoD. Null Mysteriis for example, are typically not on a crusade to rid the world of anything. Dig up some of Wood's old forum posts on RPG.net some time. Some groups (The Union, The Lucifuge) were explicitly designed as heroes, others are Ashwood Abbey and The Cheiron Group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T04:42:48-07:00","id":98266,"title":"","content":"I see the vigil as a pressure valve for mortal predation. The more predation the likely chance someone is going to take up the vigil and fight back. So most hunters already have chosen enemies, or a direction to their personal war. They handle that first whether its just keeping their homestead safe, or purging those that control the minds of society. If they handle what drew them to the vigil they may pick up other targets. A good way of doing that is finding others on the Vigil and wiping out what they are fighting. And then you can have those who developed a skill for investigation. They will pick up patterns that reveal anomalous behavior, such as anemia, amnesia, hallucinations ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:09:16-07:00","id":102834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/92387-ways-hunters-hear-about-targets#post92387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been kinda struggling, here: How do Hunters find out about targets they need to take out without that information being super public? For Conspiracies, it's a little more straight forward, since they can simply receive orders or have relatively vast networks of information gathering. But for Compacts, it seems a little more rough -- do they just have their ear pressed firmly to the ground, with a multitude of local contacts, or do they rely on &quot;suspicious&quot; news reports and so forth? If the latter, how is it they can tell something's amiss without it basically being public knowledge that something odd is happening? Or is that just the basic reality of the World of Darkness: people don't want to know that something is wrong, so they ignore it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Hunters have acquire contacts either through their professional lives or on the Vigil who tend to approach him for &quot;weird shit&quot;. An informal network starts to build over time until a ton of people know that the Hunter has a habit of making weird shit go away or at-least manageable (fun fact: this is how criminal organizations start as well!). Spread this out over the cell members and boom! you have a massive amount of people unknowingly working as feelers for the cell.<br /> <br /> It also helps that Hunters tend to develop a sense for &quot;weird shit&quot; the long they stay on the Vigil. Not so much to warrant an actual merit but rather being able to read the news line, pick out the bullshit from the truth, and decide if it's worth doing their own investigation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/92387-ways-hunters-hear-about-targets?p=94510#post94510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a highly accurate statement which needs to be kept firmly in mind when playing and running Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually the opposite. Hell, the professional training merit which is arguable the most important part of Hunter goes against that statement. Hunters are scary to monsters for a lot of reasons but the most important one is the ability to blend into society at large. Sure, you may have some Network Zero hunter screaming that monsters are among us but you also have the university professor who keeps a relic under his desk, a day laborer who knows exactly how much cement is needed to entomb a vampire, an occultist who knows just enough to fuck with odd Mage, and more. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 03-31-2014, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T13:46:23-07:00","id":102909,"title":"","content":"I think they're exaggerating for effect. I take the 'paranoid fuckwit' comment to mean that Hunters have a tendency to see all kinds of threats to themselves which may not be there, because Hunters that don't do so tend to live short lives, and also they don't often have much choice. Paranoia is useful when there really are monsters chasing you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:26:55-07:00","id":102933,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure they are actually, and even as an exaduration it's wrong since so many hunters aren't really trying to kill anything - so you can't exadurate that into a crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T04:41:29-07:00","id":103302,"title":"","content":"Well, i was actually exaggerating a bit. I realise that not every Hunter is your average &quot;Kill everything that isn't 100% human and burn the bodies!&quot; kinda guy, and some dont even want to specifically kill things. I was just trying to get across, that the very premise of Hunter is that you're slightly mentally unhinged. Thats the very idea behind the entire &quot;Risking Willpower&quot; thing, and other ways the Hunters can utilise Willpower that others cant. Their sheer force of will, and allmost borderline insane zeal for the Hunt, is what allows them to do these almost inhuman feats through sheer force of will!<br /> I agree. Hunter is very diverse. But this borderline insane conviction is common to all Hunters. So no matter what specific way your own personal crusade might play out, I'de still say you're on one form of crusade or the other. The book calls it a Vigil, but I'm more inclined to call it a crusade. Vigil has a too positive cling to it, if you ask me. Though I feel that, one way or the other, a Hunters Vigil usually ends up ridding the world of nasties, even if thats not specifically what he set out to do. Unless of course he starts making all kinds of deals with them, but we're not taking the &quot;Slasher-In-The-Making&quot; into account here. And yes, I was also refering to the habit of seeing the supernatural in places where it might not be<br /> <br /> Hunter isn't a gameline that really a specific thing that the game is about. If you're a member of the the Cheiron Group the game might be about corporate greed run amok, and an unfeeling unthinking mechanical entity made up of a hundred million little cogs, who all have the capacity for empathy and emotion, of which you are but a single one. If you're a member of the Promethean Brotherhood the game might be about forbidden knowledge, the responsibillity of having vast knowledge and power, and the price you're willing to pay for it. If you're a Lucifuge the game might be about Faustian bargains, Infernal hellfire, and trying to balance an inherently sinful birthrite, with the morals you've been raised with.<br /> .<br /> Ultimately, I supose you're right. Not every Crusade is about killings things and not every crusade is specifically about ridding the world of anything. But both of those things are in there, and they hold a pretty big thematic grip on the game, none the less. I am in staunch opposition that anything to be truely &quot;wrong&quot; in this line of game, because ultimately its our own enjoyment that comes in first line, beyond thematic apropriateness. Hunter is very diverse. And what I wrote does apply to Hunter, and so does a million other things. You were right. Its not JUST about being a crazy whackjob on a kill-spree, but its also not JUST about not being a crazy whackjob on a kill-spree. I didn't really say it was any of those things, but i understand if thats the impression i gave off.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant...<br /> <br /> Cheers ~ Krobeles<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}